[{"id":"30121","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>By the seventh century, there were big landlords or warrior chiefs in different regions of the subcontinent. Existing kings often acknowledged them as their _____.</span></p>","option_1":"Ratans","option_2":"samantas","option_3":"lakras","option_4":"hiravas","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - samantas.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>By the seventh century AD, with the decline of centralized Gupta authority, powerful landlords and warrior chiefs called \"samantas\" emerged in different regions of the Indian subcontinent. Existing kings often acknowledged these samantas as subordinate allies or vassals, who in turn paid tribute and provided military support, marking the rise of a more decentralized, feudal-like political structure in early medieval India.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30122","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>In the context of mixed economy of India, \"For whom to produce\" is decided by _____ in the economy.</span></p>","option_1":"market forces alone","option_2":"a combination of market forces and government intervention","option_3":"general agreement on tariff and trade","option_4":"government alone","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - a combination of market forces and government intervention.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>India follows a mixed economic system, where both the private sector (market forces) and the public sector (government) play significant roles in economic decision-making. In such an economy, the question \"for whom to produce\" is decided jointly by market demand-supply forces along with government policies aimed at ensuring equitable distribution and social welfare, unlike a pure capitalist economy where market forces alone decide this.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30123","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>In which year did India established its first Export Processing Zone (EPZ)?</span></p>","option_1":"1965","option_2":"1969","option_3":"1978","option_4":"1984","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - 1965.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>India established its first Export Processing Zone (EPZ) in Kandla, Gujarat, in 1965. It was the first EPZ not only in India but in all of Asia, set up to promote exports by providing a duty-free enclave with special incentives for export-oriented units.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30124","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>In which of the following places Baba Guru Nanak was born?</span></p>","option_1":"Kashi","option_2":"Talwandi","option_3":"Ayodhya","option_4":"Pandharpur","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Talwandi.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Baba Guru Nanak, the founder of Sikhism, was born in 1469 at Talwandi (now known as Nankana Sahib, located in present-day Pakistan). The place was later renamed Nankana Sahib in his honour and is considered one of the most sacred sites in Sikhism.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30125","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>All the weather phenomena like rainfall, fog and hailstorm occur in _____.</span></p>","option_1":"Exosphere","option_2":"Stratosphere","option_3":"Mesosphere","option_4":"Troposphere","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"4","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option D - Troposphere.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The troposphere is the lowest layer of the atmosphere, extending up to about 8-18 km from the Earth's surface, and it is where nearly all weather phenomena such as rainfall, fog, clouds, and hailstorms occur, since it contains most of the atmosphere's water vapour and is directly heated by the Earth's surface.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30126","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following statement is correct regarding Majuli?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>I. It is the largest inhabited riverine island in the world.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>II. It is in the Indus river.</span></p>","option_1":"Only I","option_2":"Only II","option_3":"Both I and II","option_4":"Neither I nor II","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Only I.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Majuli, located in Assam, is the largest inhabited riverine island in the world, situated in the Brahmaputra river (not the Indus river). Hence, Statement I is correct, while Statement II is factually incorrect since Majuli lies in the Brahmaputra, not the Indus.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30127","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which modern city was known as 'Saket' during Chandragupta I's rule?</span></p>","option_1":"Ujjain","option_2":"Ayodhya","option_3":"Patna","option_4":"Nashik","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Ayodhya.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>During the rule of Chandragupta I (founder of the Gupta Empire), the city known today as Ayodhya was referred to as 'Saket'. It later gained prominence as a major centre of the Gupta Empire and holds religious significance as the birthplace of Lord Rama.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30128","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following is part of the Union List of the Indian Constitution?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>I. Prison</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>II. War and Peace</span></p>","option_1":"Only I","option_2":"Only II","option_3":"Both I and II","option_4":"Neither I nor II","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Only II.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Under the Seventh Schedule of the Indian Constitution, \"Prisons\" is listed in the State List (List II), meaning states have jurisdiction over prison administration, while \"War and Peace\" is listed in the Union List (List I), as matters of defence and international relations fall under the exclusive domain of the Central Government. Hence, only \"War and Peace\" is part of the Union List.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30129","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>'Bolak-aat' is a folk dance of which of the following Indian state?</span></p>","option_1":"Gujarat","option_2":"Karnataka","option_3":"Punjab","option_4":"West Bengal","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Karnataka.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>'Bolak-aat' is a traditional folk dance form associated with Karnataka, performed to celebrate agricultural and cultural festivities, reflecting the rich folk heritage of the state.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30130","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following condition might require someone to reduce their sugar intake and take insulin injections?</span></p>","option_1":"Goitre","option_2":"Dwarfism","option_3":"Diabetes","option_4":"Scurvy","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Diabetes.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Diabetes is a chronic condition where the body either does not produce enough insulin or cannot effectively use the insulin it produces, leading to high blood sugar levels. Management typically requires reducing sugar and carbohydrate intake and, in many cases (especially Type 1 diabetes or advanced Type 2), taking insulin injections to regulate blood glucose levels.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30131","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>'Agalmaka festival' is celebrated in which Indian state?</span></p>","option_1":"Kerala","option_2":"Gujarat","option_3":"Meghalaya","option_4":"Andhra Pradesh","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Meghalaya.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The 'Agalmaka festival' is celebrated in Meghalaya, reflecting the cultural traditions of the indigenous tribal communities of the state, which include rituals, dance, and music tied to agricultural and social life.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30132","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>In the Socio Economic and Caste Census (SECC) 2011, how many deprivation criteria was there?</span></p>","option_1":"5","option_2":"7","option_3":"11","option_4":"12","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - 7.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The Socio Economic and Caste Census (SECC) 2011 identified households based on seven deprivation criteria (such as households with no adult member aged 16-59, female-headed households with no adult male member, households with a disabled member and no able-bodied adult, SC/ST households, landless households deriving major income from manual labour, etc.) to identify automatically included/excluded and deprived households for welfare scheme targeting.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30133","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following is correct regarding fluid friction?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>I. When objects move through fluids they lose energy due to it.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>II. It can be minimised by giving suitable shapes to bodies moving in fluids.</span></p>","option_1":"Only I","option_2":"Only II","option_3":"Both I and II","option_4":"Neither I nor II","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Both I and II.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Fluid friction (or drag) causes objects moving through fluids (liquids or gases) to lose kinetic energy, which is converted into heat due to resistance from the fluid — making Statement I correct. This drag can be minimised by streamlining the shape of the object (as seen in the design of cars, aircraft, and fish bodies), making Statement II correct as well. Hence, both statements are correct.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30134","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The Navigation with Indian Constellation (NavIC) coverage area includes India and a region up to _____ km beyond the Indian boundary.</span></p>","option_1":"1500","option_2":"4000","option_3":"6500","option_4":"7000","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - 1500.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>NavIC (Navigation with Indian Constellation), India's indigenous satellite navigation system developed by ISRO, is designed to provide accurate position information covering India and a region extending up to 1,500 km beyond its borders.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30135","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>What is the name of Google's seventh-generation AI chip designed primarily for inference in April 2025?</span></p>","option_1":"Trillium","option_2":"Ironwood","option_3":"Gemini TPU","option_4":"AlphaCore","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option