m:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The term \"Ippon\" is related to which of the following sports?</span></p>","option_1":"Badminton","option_2":"Kabaddi","option_3":"Judo","option_4":"Kho-Kho","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Judo.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>\"Ippon\" is a term used in Judo, signifying a full point awarded for a decisive technique (such as a perfect throw, pin, or submission) that instantly ends the match, similar to a \"knockout\" in other combat sports.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30141","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following book has been written by Jawaharlal Nehru and it shows a broad view of Indian history, culture and philosophy?</span></p>","option_1":"The Ancient Wisdom","option_2":"Indian Struggle","option_3":"The Discovery of India","option_4":"History of Indian Philosophy","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - The Discovery of India.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>\"The Discovery of India\" is a book written by Jawaharlal Nehru during his imprisonment at Ahmednagar Fort in 1944, offering a broad and reflective view of Indian history, culture, and philosophy from ancient times to the modern era, and remains one of his most celebrated literary works.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30142","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"790","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following is NOT a Jumping event in sports?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>I. Pole Vault</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>II. Discus Throw</span></p>","option_1":"Only I","option_2":"Only II","option_3":"Both I and II","option_4":"Neither I nor II","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","optio